+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action and reusable workflow version pinning
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: owner/action@main
+  call:
+    uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@v1
+```
+
+`action-pinning: {}` is configured for this output.
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:6:15: step action reference "owner/action@main" is not pinned at the required "semver" level [action-pinning]
+  |
+6 |       - uses: owner/action@main
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:8:11: reusable workflow reference "owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@v1" is not pinned at the required "semver" level [action-pinning]
+  |
+8 |     uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/ci.yml@v1
+  |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+This opt-in rule checks remote references in step-level action `uses:` and job-level reusable workflow `uses:`. Configure it
+with the [`action-pinning` section](config.md) or enable it with `-action-pinning-level`. The available levels, from least to
+most strict, are `major-minor`, `semver`, and `commit-sha`. A ref satisfying a stricter level also satisfies a less strict level.
+
+Local references starting with `./` and Docker references starting with `docker://` are not checked. References whose action
+name contains an expression are skipped. When the action name is static but the ref is an expression, actionlint reports that
+the ref cannot be verified.
+
